# VContainer & dependency injection

**When:** Adding injectable services, MonoBehaviours, entry points, or ScriptableObject config to the game.

## Single root scope

- Only application scope: `GameLifetimeScope` (`Assets/_Project/Systems/Core/VContainer/Scripts/GameLifetimeScope.cs`) — declared `partial`.
- Bootstrapped via `Assets/_Project/Settings/VContainerSettings.asset` → `RootLifetimeScope` field, pointing at `Assets/_Project/Systems/Core/VContainer/Prefabs/GameLifetimeScope.prefab`.
- `Configure` calls **three** generated entry points: `builder.RegisterAutoGenerated()`, `RegisterGeneratedPrefabs(builder)`, `_scriptableObjects.Register(builder)`. No hand-written `builder.Register…` calls exist today.
- **Do not** add `IInstaller` classes or extra `LifetimeScope` subclasses unless the task explicitly requires a child scope.

## Auto-registration (preferred)

Attributes in `VContainer.AutoRegistration`; Roslyn emits `{Scope}_AutoGenerated.g.cs` (`RegisterAutoGenerated`) and `{Scope}_SerializedContainers.g.cs` (`RegisterGeneratedPrefabs` + nested `VContainerScriptableObjects`). **No runtime assembly scan.**

| What | Attribute | Notes |
|------|-----------|--------|
| Plain C# service | `[RegisterIn(typeof(GameLifetimeScope))]` + `[RegisterAs(typeof(I…))]` | Default lifetime = Singleton |
| Transient / Scoped | `[RegisterIn(scope, Lifetime.Transient)]` | Second arg on `RegisterIn` |
| All interfaces | `[AsImplementedInterfaces]` | Wins over `[RegisterAs]` if both present |
| Also as concrete | `[RegisterAsSelf]` | Adds `.AsSelf()` alongside `[RegisterAs]` / `[AsImplementedInterfaces]` |
| PlayerLoop hook (plain C#) | `[RegisterEntryPointIn(typeof(GameLifetimeScope))]` | For `IStartable` / `ITickable` on **non-MonoBehaviour** types; always Singleton |
| Scene `MonoBehaviour` | `[RegisterComponentIn(scope, ComponentSource.Hierarchy)]` | Component must exist in hierarchy at resolve time |
| Prefab `MonoBehaviour` | `[RegisterComponentIn(scope, ComponentSource.Prefab, parentGameObjectName: "Folder")]` | Generates a `[SerializeField]` slot on the `partial` scope; assign on **Prefabs** tab |
| ScriptableObject | `[RegisterInstanceIn(scope)]` + `[RegisterAs(...)]` | Singleton only; assign on **Scriptable Objects** tab |

**Consume** via constructor injection (`IEventPublisher`, `ICommandDispatcher`, `ICommandHistory`, etc.). Don't use `[Inject]` fields except on types resolved through the container — `CommandDispatcher` calls `IObjectResolver.Inject(command)` on each dispatch, so `[Inject]` fields/properties on command classes are the documented path.

## Commands are NOT container types

Instantiate per dispatch; the dispatcher injects via `IObjectResolver.Inject(command)`. **Never** apply `[RegisterIn]` to a command class.

## Manual registration

`GameLifetimeScope.Configure` currently has none. Add `builder.Register…` lines **only** for types the generator can't express. VContainer auto-resolves `IReadOnlyList<T>` from any registered `T`, so collection bindings (e.g. `IDispatchPolicy`) need no manual setup.

## Anti-patterns

- `[RegisterIn]` on `MonoBehaviour` → use `[RegisterComponentIn]` (diagnostic VCAR003)
- Prefab registration on a non-`partial` scope → VCAR001
- `[RegisterAs(typeof(I))]` when the class doesn't implement `I` → VCAR004
- `IStartable` on prefab MB with `[AsImplementedInterfaces]` unless PlayerLoop hooks are intentional
- Duplicate attribute + manual `Register` for the same type
- Editing `*_AutoGenerated.g.cs` / `*_SerializedContainers.g.cs`

